// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -emit-llvm -output %t >> /dev/null 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=CIR %s --input-file %t.cir
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=LL %s --input-file %t.ll

// Real Ghidra 12.0.4 ground-truth output for an AArch64 freestanding ELF
// whose every public function executes one AArch64 synchronization
// instruction (DMB / DSB / ISB / CLREX) or simple LL/SC load (LDXR /
// LDAXR / LDAR). Source: firmwares/atomics-probe/atomics_probe_aarch64.c.
//
// Stock Ghidra emits these CALLOTHER intrinsic targets in this fixture:
// DataMemoryBarrier, DataSynchronizationBarrier,
// InstructionSynchronizationBarrier, ClearExclusiveLocal. The exclusive
// loads (LDXR / LDAXR / LDAR) are lifted as inline LOAD without surfacing
// a CALLOTHER userop, so they exercise the unmodified load path. STXR /
// STLXR are deliberately omitted from the probe because ClangIR's CIRGen
// has not yet implemented the bitcast-on-function-return-value path that
// the resulting CAST chain requires.

// Normalized canonical intrinsics:
// CIR-DAG: @atomic_thread_fence_seq_cst
